<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/100102> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The ZNU standard for sustainable management helps companies to become more sustainable step by step and calls for continuous improvement. The standard integrates all three dimensions of environment, economy and social issues and requires the development of an integrated management system for more sustainable management. The requirements of the ZNU standard for sustainable management are divided into two parts:  (1) sustainable corporate management (“How do you design sustainable corporate management?”) and (2) sustainability issues (“What exactly are you doing?”).  The ZNU Standard – driving sustainable change is site specific but requires a comprehensive evaluation of the company’s impact on value chain and society. Orientation towards individual issues such as climate, packaging (environmental implications), innovation, fair payment (economic implications) or human rights and diversity (social implications) ensures and fosters a dynamic and effective process of learning and development in the company, which in turn stimulates innovative lateral and circular thinking in the sense of a circular process of economy.  https://www.znu-standard.com/en/the-znu-standard  ZNU is a site-specific management system standard (e.g. only those products are referred to which are produced at the certified site.  https://www.znu-standard.com/fileadmin/media-znu-standard/006_Download/Englisch/Z6_Rules_of_communication_ZNU_2018_.pdf https://www.znu-standard.com/fileadmin/media-znu-standard/006_Download/Englisch/Z1_Objectives_and_overviews_ZNU_2018_.pdf" ;
  dct:issued "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:references <https://www.znu-standard.com/en/the-znu-standard> ;
  dct:relation <https://www.znu-standard.com/en/downloads>, <https://www.znu-standard.com/en/the-znu-standard> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/100102> ;
  dct:title "ZNU Standard - driving sustainable change" ;
