  eudpp:valueChain <https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/Value_Chain/Distribution>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/Value_Chain/Manufacturing>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/thesauri/Value_Chain/Production> .

<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/119> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Headquartered in Arlington, Virginia, USA, with regional offices in Hong Kong, SAR, and Dhaka, Bangladesh, full-time staff in Europe, India, and Southeast Asia (Thailand, Vietnam and Indonesia), and for Latin America and Africa and Middle East, WRAP is an independent, objective, non-profit team of global social compliance experts dedicated to promoting safe, lawful, humane, and ethical manufacturing around the world through certification and education.    Our primary activity is our Certification Program, which is the largest independent facility certification program in the world mainly focused on sewn-products and related sectors, including apparel, footwear, home textile, fashion accessories, mills, leather, travel goods, cashmere, silk, printing  and home accessories. We issue three levels of certification that are valid for one year or two years based on a facility's compliance with WRAP's 12 Principles. These principles are based on generally accepted international workplace standards, local laws, and workplace regulations, and include the spirit or language of the relevant conventions of the International Labor Organization (ILO), the United Nations Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights, and the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD)'s Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises.    WRAP also administers a comprehensive training program throughout the world. Some courses are also accredited by Association of Professional Social Compliance Auditors (APSCA) to fulfill APSCA auditors' annual requirements for Continuing Professional Development (CPD). All of our monitoring partners must undergo our comprehensive Five-Day Auditor Training program and follow-up with regular refresher courses. We also offer an Internal Monitoring Course which teaches factory managers and workers how to make their facilities compliant with our 12 Principles. Additionally, WRAP has been a pioneer in Factory Fire Safety Training, offering the course in Bangladesh, Pakistan, China, India, and Southeast Asia." ;
  dct:issued "2000"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <http://www.wrapcompliance.org/en/12-principles>, <https://wrapcompliance.org/certification/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/119> ;
  dct:title "Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production - WRAP" ;
