<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/128> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "SMETA is a responsible supply chain audit methodology launched by Sedex and is applicable to all sectors. SMETA can be used to evaluate and measure the social and environmental compliance of the company/site or supply chain. A full SMETA audit covers four pillars of Health & Safety, Labour, Environment and Business Ethics, for a comprehensive review of a worksite’s sustainability practices. It is a combination of in-person scrutiny and scalable methodology for businesses to draw comparable data on sustainability practices, conditions, workers and risks at individual worksites in supply chains." ;
  dct:issued "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/128> ;
  dct:title "SMETA Audit" ;
