<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/131> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The Responsible jewelry Council (RJC) is a sustainability standards and certification initiative for the jewelry and watch supply chain, unique in that organizations at every step in the value chain (from mine to retail) participates. The RJC Code of Practices defines the requirements for responsible business practices throughout the jewelry and watch supply chain, from mine to retail. It provides a common standard for ethical, social, human rights and environmental practices. COP certification is mandatory for all our commercial members. The RJC Chain-of-Custody Standard defines an approach for companies to handle and trade gold, silver and platinum group metals in a way that is traceable and responsibly sourced. CoC certification is voluntary and complements certification against our COP, which is mandatory for all members." ;
  dct:issued "2005"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.responsiblejewelry.com/standards/chain-of-custody-2017/>, <https://www.responsiblejewelry.com/standards/code-of-practices-2019/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/131> ;
  dct:title "Responsible jewelry Council (RJC)" ;
