<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/155> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "China environmental labeling program is a public voluntary eco-label scheme, initiated by State Environmental Protection Administration (Now Ministry of Ecology and Environment, China-MEE) in 1994, aiming to encourage the businesses to rationally use resources and energy to develop and produce environment-friendly products, guide the consumers to choose and identify green products towards sustainable consumption, and provides a way for the businesses and public to self-consciously participate in environmental protection.Ministry of Ecology and Environment of China (MEE) owns the China Environmental Labeling and China Environmental United Certification Center (CEC) undertakes the function of Product certification.In 2010, MEE launched low-carbon product certification, which is based on the framework of China environmental labeling." ;
  dct:issued "1994"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/155> ;
  dct:title "China Environmental Labeling" ;
