<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/164> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "In 2010, the largest CSR supply chain auditing and certification body, Intertek, set out to challenge norms on scheduling, tracking, conducting and reporting on social responsibility audits.  Rooted in 20 years of experience in supply chain auditing for CSR performance, the Workplace Conditions Assessment (WCA) is a data driven, software-based community platform that enables automated data collection leading to ratings based measurable audit results. Auditors are provided an efficient and streamlined audit format based on Intertek’s leading eAudit technology, and brand/retailer users of the WCA have access to invaluable data mining tools that can help set performance metrics which are capable of being benchmarked against global, industry, and country averages." ;
  dct:issued "2010"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/164> ;
  dct:title "Workplace Condition Assessment (WCA)" ;
