<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/167> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "IFS Food applies when products are “processed” or when there is a hazard for product contamination during primary packing. The Standard is important for all food manufacturers, especially for those producing private labels, as it contains many requirements related to the compliance with customer specifications.  The Standard supports the production and marketing departments in their efforts for brand safety and quality. IFS Food has been developed with full and active involvement of certification bodies, retailers, food industry and food service companies.  It covers six primary areas of the business, and all are considered key to establishing effective processes that guarantee the safety and quality of the products; 1) Governance and Commitment 2) Food Safety and Quality Management System 3) Resource Management  4) Operational Processes 5) Measurements, Analysis, and Improvements 6) Food defense Plan" ;
  dct:issued "2003"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.ifs-certification.com/images/standards/ifs_food7/documents/standards/IFS_Food_v7_standard_en.pdf> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/167> ;
  dct:title "IFS Food" ;
