<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/175> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The Biosphere Methodology is the only international system to apply continuous improvement processes, connected in real-time to the 17 SDGs and 169 targets of the United Nations and indicators developed with the UNSDSN.    It is based on the 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, focusing initiatives on the certification process around the three fundamental pillars of sustainability, which are grouped into “Environment and Climate Change”, “Society and Culture”, “Governance and Economy”. Each of these areas is directly linked to several Sustainable Development Goals, thus defining the requirements to obtain the Biosphere certification.   The Biosphere system is conducted 100% online, through a digital platform that offers two different distinctions: 1. Biosphere Committed, as a membership distinction to be part of the Biosphere Community, after passing an initial online evaluation on basic sustainability issues connected with the SDGs. 2. Biosphere Certified, which demonstrates compliance with more rigorous criteria, after passing a 100% online third-party external audit, where the level of compliance required for the SDGs and sustainability areas is much higher.   The process is very simple: create a personalized and individual Sustainability Plan for each entity, where you select the sustainable activities and actions you wish to address voluntarily. From Biosphere, they provide all the know-how through their platform so you can identify the actions already considered in your business strategies and the levels of your indicators. Biosphere’s system also propose a set of initiatives that you can implement to advance in your journey toward continuous improvement, always in line with your reality, resources, goals, and interests, linking all the information and best practices with the 169 targets and 17 Sustainable Development Goals of the UN. It is a truly flexible, adaptable, and scalable system for any company, regardless of its type or size." ;
  dct:issued "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.biospheretourism.com/en> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/175> ;
  dct:title "Biosphere Certification for Companies Responsible Tourism Institute" ;
