<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/2099> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "In 2019, BRCGS launched the Ethical Trade and Responsible Sourcing Program (ETRS) which is made up of a Global Standard and a separate ETRS Risk Assessment.  The Standard’s requirements span six principles, giving sites a framework on which they can build their own ethical trade and responsible sourcing management system. This enables them to ensure their legal obligations are fulfilled, their premises are safe, healthy and do not harm those working in or visiting them and that their staff’s employment and human rights are respected, whether they are temporary or permanent.  The ETRS Risk Assessment is designed to be a diagnostic ‘health check’ against the five vital signs of ethical trade and responsible sourcing which are drawn from the Global Standard. Issue 2.1 of the BRCGS Ethical Trade and Responsible Sourcing (ETRS) Global Standard was published in June 2023" ;
  dct:issued "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.brcgs.com/product/global-standard-ethical-trade-and-responsible-sourcing-issue-2-1/p-19031/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/2099> ;
  dct:title "BRCGS Ethical Trade and Responsible Sourcing" ;
