<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/21> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The FairWild Foundation was established to promote the sustainable management and supply chain development of wild-collected natural ingredients and products. FairWild Foundation maintains the FairWild Standard and certification scheme for sustainable collection and fair trade in these ingredients.  The FairWild Standard provides guidance on best-practice harvesting and trading of wild-harvested plant, fungi and lichen ingredients. It forms the basis of a third-party audited certification scheme, available for wild collection operations worldwide. Traders and brand manufacturers may register with FairWild Foundation to trade FairWild-certified ingredients and label finished products with the FairWild mark, under license agreement." ;
  dct:issued "2008"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <http://www.fairwild.org/documents> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/21> ;
  dct:title "FairWild " ;
