<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/21100101> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Biosphere is the international system of the Responsible Tourism Institute (RTI), an organization founded with the support of UNESCO through an MoU in 1995. The only international system for implementing continuous improvement processes, connected in real time with the 17 SDGs and 169 United Nations targets, along with indicators tailored specifically to your destination, thanks to the methodological collaboration between the RTI and UN-SDSN.   It is based on the 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, focusing initiatives on the certification process around the three fundamental pillars of sustainability, which are grouped into “Environment and Climate Change”, “Society and Culture”, “Governance and Economy”. Each of these areas is directly linked to several Sustainable Development Goals, thus defining the requirements to obtain the Biosphere certification.   The Biosphere system is conducted 100% online, through a digital platform that integrates and connects the sustainability efforts of all stakeholders, bringing them together: destinations, institutions, companies, clients, employees, travelers, and citizens." ;
  dct:created "2022-01-19"^^xsd:date ;
  dct:issued "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/21100101> ;
  dct:title "Biosphere Certification for destinations" ;
