<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/215> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Formed in 1996 by Kenyan growers and exporters of cut-flowers, Kenya Flower Council is a business membership organization that advocates for interests and represents 80% of the flower industry in Kenya.  At its formation, KFC’s initial membership stood at 5 farm and has continuously grown to 130 large, medium and small producers and 93 associate members that provide essential services to the sector in Kenya." ;
  dct:issued "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/215> ;
  dct:title "Flowers and Ornamentals Sustainability Standard - KFC Gold and Silver Level" ;
