<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/237> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The EO100™ Standard for Responsible Energy is a set of rigorous performance standards for energy development projects. The EO100™ Standard is the product of extensive consultation with the energy industry, leading international NGOs focused on energy, and indigenous communities affected by development projects. With several assurance options available, EO100™ can be applied as an internal benchmarking tool and for social and environmental performance management. It can also be used for investment and supply-chain due diligence. Third-party verification of compliance with all parameters of the EO100™ Standard at a specific energy development site (e.g. an oil or gas drilling pad, a hydroelectric dam, or a wind farm) earns the site EO Certification." ;
  dct:issued "2009"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <http://www.equitableorigin.org/eo100-for-responsible-energy/overview/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/237> ;
  dct:title "EO100TM Standard for Responsible Energy Development" ;
