<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/263> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The FAO Guidelines: Sustainability Assessment of Food and Agriculture systems (SAFA), provide an international reference for sustainable management, monitoring and reporting in food and agriculture at all levels of the supply chain. SAFA is not a sustainability index, nor a sustainability standard, nor a labelling tool. SAFA: defines what sustainable food and agriculture systems are, including environmental  integrity, economic resilience, social well-being and good governance; outlines a procedure for an integrated analysis of all dimensions of sustainability,  including the selection of appropriate indicators and rating of sustainability  performance (best, good, moderate, limited, unacceptable); and  describes sustainability themes, sub-themes  and indicators.  SAFA is objective-oriented. Indicators are designed to fulfil the Theme’s goals and the Sub-Themes objectives. Thus, individual practices are addressed only implicitly in term of their achievement of the stated objectives." ;
  dct:issued "2013"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <http://www.fao.org/fileadmin/templates/nr/sustainability_pathways/docs/SAFA_Indicators_final_19122013.pdf> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/263> ;
  dct:title "Sustainability Assessment of Food and Agriculture systems - SAFA" ;
