<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/278> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Naturland Fair certification is a voluntary supplementary option for Naturland certified producers’ organizations, individual producers and processors.  Naturland Fair combines the values of organic, social, regional and global fair trade and fills them with life. In doing so, Naturland embraces producers and consumers in all parts of the world and addresses the global north as the global south. As an organic association of growers and as a partner of both processing as well as trading enterprises, Naturland Fair aims at connecting all the players involved in food production. In doing so, it creates a sector of genuinely sustainable economic activity throughout the entire value chain. Certification to the Naturland Fair standards makes a contribution towards improving farmers’ livelihoods and securing the existence of organic agricultural operations." ;
  dct:issued "1982"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.naturland.de/images/01_naturland/_en/Documents/Documents_Producers/01_Certification/01_ICS_MinReq/ICS_Naturland_Manual_AnnexVIII_MinimumRequirements.pdf>, <https://www.naturland.de/images/01_naturland/_en/Standards/Naturland-Standards-on-Production.pdf>, <https://www.naturland.de/images/01_naturland/_en/Standards/Naturland-Standards_Extract-Social-responsibility.pdf>, <https://www.naturland.de/images/01_naturland/_en/Standards/Naturland-Standards_Fair.pdf> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/278> ;
  dct:title "Naturland Fair" ;
  eudpp:appliesToCountryOfDestination <https://w3id.org/eudpp/country/AT>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/country/DE>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/country/PH> ;
