<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/284> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The Global Recycled Standard is introduced by Textile Exchange, a non-profit organization that promotes a more sustainable supply chain of textile production. The standard contains environmental requirements for textile manufacturing companies and ensures the traceability of materials used during the production process. Labeled products contain at least 20% recycled materials. The standard therefore mainly focuses on the production of fibers." ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/284> ;
  dct:title "Global Recycled Standard - GRS" ;
