<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/288> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Fairtrade Standards seek to ensure fairer terms of trade between farmers and buyers, protect workers’ rights, and provide the framework for producers to build thriving farms and organizations. The key objectives of the Fairtrade Standards are to:   •\tEnsure that producers receive prices that cover their average costs of sustainable production.   •\tProvide an additional Fairtrade Premium which can be invested in projects that enhance social, economic, and environmental development.   •\tEnable pre-financing for producers who require it.   •\tFacilitate long-term trading partnerships and enable greater producer control over the trading process.   •\tSet clear core and development criteria to ensure that the conditions of production and trade of all Fairtrade certified products are both socially and economically fair as well as environmentally responsible." ;
  dct:issued "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.fairtrade.net/standard/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/288> ;
  dct:title "Fairtrade standard for Fibre crops" ;
