<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/387653> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Green Shape is an environmental standard for apparel and textile outdoor products that has been developed by VAUDE Sport GmbH & Co. KG since 2010. The motivation for this was the lack of a suitable standard that could reflect the specific requirements of an environmentally friendly product portfolio. At the same time, there was a growing desire from retailers to make more environmentally friendly products visible and recognizable to consumers. Initially developed for internal processes, Green Shape has since been further developed in several review stages and is now being opened up to the wider market. Today, the standard takes into account all phases of the product life cycle - from design, material selection and production to use and disposal. It has been continuously developed with regard to the circular economy and environmental impact in the supply chain.   The \"Green Shape Verein zur Förderung umweltfreundlicher Bekleidung und textiler Produkte e.V.\" (Green Shape e.V.) was founded at the beginning of 2025 as a new programme owner of the Green Shape Standard that is independent of VAUDE. This non-profit, registered association has developed the Green Shape Standard into a fully-fledged certification system.     The Green Shape Standard is currently undergoing program testing at the German Accreditation Body (DAkkS). An application has been made to register the Green Shape logo as an EU certification mark.     The aim is to establish this standard as a new, credible and ambitious environmental certification for the textile and outdoor industry in line with the EU's anti-greenwashing requirements." ;
  dct:created "2022-08-09"^^xsd:date ;
  dct:issued "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://green-shape.org/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/387653> ;
  dct:title "Green Shape" ;
