<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/40> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The Ethical Supply Chain Program (ESCP), (formerly ICTI Ethical Toy Program), was founded by the International Council of Toy Industries in 2004 and now champions integrity and sustainability across all sectors. It exists as an independent, not-for profit organization dedicated to improving ethical standards at factories around the world, including in relation to ethics, non-discrimination, employment practices, and environment and chemical safety, among others. The organization facilitates communication, certification and cooperation between manufacturers, suppliers and retailers worldwide to build a network with transparency at its core. But it’s much more than an ethical rubber stamp: it is a commitment to respect, fairness, and inclusivity. ESCP offers certification, assessment, and monitoring tools to achieve responsible sourcing aims and drive standards, with the aim of creating a better life for workers worldwide. This includes the development and implementation of the Factory Certification Program and other programs which provide assurance regarding labor standards. Additionally, ECSP offers its Social Impact Assessment, Environmental Assessment and a wide range of capability-building programs, along with scalable worker wellbeing initiatives, all with the aim of creating a better life for workers worldwide." ;
  dct:issued "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.ethicalSupply> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/40> ;
  dct:title "Ethical Supply Chain Program" ;
