<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/408> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "3S Program™ (Responsible Production Verified) is Cargill’s own sustainability certification program. It has been developed to support farmers grow more sustainable soy.   3S takes key sustainability criteria and splits them into musts and continuous improvement actions. Over time, participating growers are able to advance towards higher production standards which in turn helps further a thriving market for sustainably certified soy. 3S is deployed using  independent sustainability specialists who visit the farms and make individual farm diagnostics. 3S is a certification scheme with no deforestation and no conversion of native habitat, using January 2008  as the baseline date.  We have 3S™ farmers in Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay." ;
  dct:relation <https://www.cargill.com/doc/1432181492104/3s-guidance-(pdf).pdf> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/408> ;
  dct:title "Cargill Triple S Soya Products" ;
