<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/435> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Bunge is a leading agribusiness and food company with integrated operations that circle the globe. We bring products from where they are grown to where they are processed to where they are consumed in a safe and sustainable way.       The company strives to promote sustainable agriculture and implement robust projects that protect and improve the environment, while supporting the social and economic well-being of growers, employees and local communities. Bunge operates with sourcing standards to secure best practices in its supply chain and Sustainable Sourcing is one the core pillars of our global sustainability platform. The platform  also comprises Action on Climate and Accountability. Learn more about our sustainability strategy at www.bunge.com/sustainability.        As stated in the Land Use and Biodiversity Policy, Bunge is ready to comply with market certification if demanded and compensated by customers. The PRO-S certification program was created in 2012, based on stakeholders consultation from 2009 to 2012 and is intended to leverage the assurance on sustainable criteria, as per market trends. Stakeholder consultation enhanced the standard in 2015, 2019 and 2021, as the standard is committed to the continuous improvement and applicability to market dynamics. It remains, though, based on criteria that include the following assurance and possibilities to customers:       \tGeographic approach: sourcing from regions of preference.   \tFarm traceability: each tonnage of product is connected to a farm of origin in Bunge’s sourcing.   \tForest footprint: no sourcing from farms that deforested after June 2016.        Labor compliance in Primary Suppliers’ farms: no association to degrading conditions for field workers, as well as child labor or discrimination.   \tNo relation to illegal activities with environmental impact.    \tRisk analysis for sensitive issues.   \tCommitment to continuous improvement.   \tUse of chemical inputs in compliance to legislation.           The standard is applicable to agricultural commodities and its derivatives. It is based on mass balance control under Bunge’s management and its operating companies. The mass balance demands physical flow of product among Bunge’s operating companies. Annual inspection by third party applies for mass balance validation and transparency of the program. The PRO-S system brings the set of indicators that better fit current demands from stakeholders and markets. The principles and criteria follow FEFAC’s (European Feed Manufacturers’ Associations) Soy Sourcing Guidelines. PRO-S is a global program, primarily focused on agricultural sourcing from Brazil. Some indicators may not apply equally in other countries where some of the topics are not material.       The PRO-S certification is available upon previous request from customer and subject to commercial agreement. It represents a differential in trading and is in compliance with the sustainability related policies implemented by Bunge." ;
  dct:issued "2012"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://delivery.bunge.com/-/media/Files/2024/PRO-S-Sustainable-Sourcing-Certification_Bunge2023.ashx> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/435> ;
  dct:title "Bunge Pro-S Assuring Sustainable Sourcing" ;
