<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/449> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The EU Ecolabel is owned by the European Commission. The European Union Eco-labelling Board (EUEB) with representatives of each EU member state as well as industry, environmental and consumer associations is responsible for the label. It aims at helping consumers to identify environmentally friendly products. The label covers the following range of products: Desktop computers and integrated desktop computers, portable all-in-one computers, notebooks, two-in-one notebook computers, tablet computers, thin clients, workstations and small-scale server. The EU Ecolabel for computer covers ecological criteria devices have to fulfill, such as recyclable design. It also addresses the origin and extraction of conflict minerals, as well as social standards during the final assembly stage of devices. All requirements of the EU Ecolabel have to be met immediately." ;
  dct:issued "1958"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://ec.europa.eu/environment/ecolabel/about_ecolabel/pdf/EUEB_rules_procedure.pdf>, <https://ec.europa.eu/environment/ecolabel/documents/EU%20Ecolabel%20Work%20plan%202020-2024%20Dec%202020.pdf>, <https://ec.europa.eu/environment/ecolabel/documents/Logo%20Guidelines_June%202020.pdf>, <https://ec.europa.eu/environment/topics/circular-economy/eu-ecolabel-home/about-eu-ecolabel_en>, <https://ec.europa.eu/environment/topics/circular-economy/eu-ecolabel-home/community-and-Help>, <https://environment.ec.europa.eu/system/files/2022-05/EU_Ecolabel_fees_table_2022_02.pdf>, <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=CELEX:32010R0066&from=EN> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/449> ;
  dct:title "EU Ecolabel - Computer" ;
