<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/470> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "Fairtrade Standards ensure fairer terms of trade between farmers and buyers, protect workers’ rights, and provide the framework for producers to build thriving farms and organizations. The key objectives of the Fairtrade Standards are to:  Ensure that producers receive prices that cover their average costs of sustainable production. Provide an additional Fairtrade Premium which can be invested in projects that enhance social, economic and environmental development. Enable pre-financing for producers who require it. Facilitate long-term trading partnerships and enable greater producer control over the trading process. Set clear core and development criteria to ensure that the conditions of production and trade of all Fairtrade certified products are both socially and economically fair as well as environmentally responsible." ;
  dct:issued "1997"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.fairtrade.net/en/why-fairtrade/how-we-do-it/fairtrade-standards/who-we-have-standards-for/textile-standard.html> ;
