<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/471> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The Austrian Ecolabel for Household & Cleaning (https://www.umweltzeichen.at/en/products/household-cleaning) provides a list of dropdown menus for license holders of different products. Included in this list is \"Laundry Detergents UZ 21\" which, when selected, provides a PDF link: \"UZ Guideline short version\". This \"UZ Guideline short version\" provides a general overview of the European Ecolabel for Laundry Detergents and contains a link to access the full detailed criteria (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=CELEX:32017D1218). The UZ Guideline short version states: Once it's on your products, the EU Ecolabel guarantees • A reduced amount of total chemicals  • Limited substances harmful to the environment • Increased biodegradability • Less packaging • An efficient wash • Reliable consumer information It can be awarded to all kinds of laundry detergents, in powder, liquid or any other form. https://www.umweltzeichen.at/file/Guideline/UZ%2021/Short/Uz21_K5a_engl.pdf Statutes of the Environmental Label Association; April 2020 5) Valid award criteria of the EU Ecolabel or the Blue Angel can also be used as the basis for a directive for the Austrian Ecolabel. In individual cases, the BMK or the third party commissioned by the BMK can present such criteria to a technical committee, which can recommend to the Advisory Board that these Ecolabel award criteria be adopted in full as a guideline for the Austrian Ecolabel.  https://www.umweltzeichen.at/site/assets/files/3072/2020_04_satzung_umweltzeichen.pdf" ;
  dct:issued "1990"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:references <https://www.umweltzeichen.at/en/products/household-cleaning)> ;
  dct:relation <https://environment.ec.europa.eu/topics/circular-economy/eu-ecolabel/product-groups-and-criteria/cleaning_en> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/471> ;
  dct:title "Austrian Ecolabel - Detergents" ;
