<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/484> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "In addition to the Nordic Swan Ecolabel for Products, national Ecolabeling regulations and statutory orders apply in each of the five Nordic countries. The Nordic Swan Ecolabel for products sets requirements that go beyond national regulations and statutory orders rather than duplicating what is set by Nordic Law. The Nordic Swan Ecolabel is administered and managed by Nordic Ecolabeling, a joint Nordic organization. Nordic Ecolabeling consists of five local organizations / companies in Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Norway and Sweden. They work tightly in fulfilling the goals of the Nordic Council of Minister. Each country has its own Ecolabeling secretariat, which is responsible for that country's activities. Each secretariat handles licence applications, inspection visits and marketing in their respective countries. Each country is also responsible for its own country's position in questions regarding product groups and criteria issues. The secretariats meet in the Nordic Ecolabeling Board for decisions on criteria and fees. https://www.nordic-swan-ecolabel.org/nordic-Ecolabeling/" ;
  dct:issued "1989"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:references <https://www.nordic-swan-ecolabel.org/nordic-Ecolabeling/> ;
  dct:relation <https://www.nordic-swan-ecolabel.org/criteria/laundry-detergents-and-stain-removers-006/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/484> ;
  dct:title "Nordic Ecolabeling for Laundry Detergents and Stain Removers" ;
