<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/547> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "4C Services GmbH is the current scheme manager and operates the 4C Certification System. 4C stands for the Common Code for the Coffee Community and the 4C Certification system operates based on the 4C Code of Conduct, that was firstly launched in September 2004 (version 1.0) as a result of a collaborative project in a public-private partnership between the German Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ) and the German Coffee Association (DKV). The 4C certification aims to gradually raise the social, economic and environmental conditions of coffee production and processing worldwide.  4C was created through a participatory, extensive, transparent and balanced consultation with coffee stakeholders worldwide." ;
  dct:issued "2016"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://portal.4c-services.org>, <https://www.4c-services.org/process/document-library/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/547> ;
  dct:title "The Common Code for the Coffee Community - 4C" ;
