<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/553> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "There is now a wide range of organic food and natural cosmetics. However, many everyday products, such as detergents and cleaning agents, household items, toys or textiles come from petrochemical manufacturing. They contain microplastics, plasticizers and other unnatural and environmentally harmful ingredients.   NCP labels those products that are made from natural ingredients and do not harm the environment: care products for objects (e.g. laundry detergent, dishwashing detergent, fabric softener or furniture polish), hygiene products (e.g. panty liners, disinfectants or anti-mosquito spray), gardening supplies (e.g. fertilizer or tools), toys (e.g. finger paints, plasticine, etc.), candles  If a natural product is certified according to the NCP standard it means that natural ingredients, such as sunflower oil are used and, furthermore, that the chemical processes during production correspond to natural processes, such as the metabolic process of a plant.   The NCP seal on a product guarantees all the properties mentioned here:  only ingredients of plant/animal origin no microplastics no genetic engineering no animal testing (except legally required) no synthetic silicones or surfactants  no radioactive irradiation purely natural fragrances and plant extracting agents certified palm oil packages from recyclable materials" ;
  dct:issued "2011"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://gfaw.eu/en/downloads/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/553> ;
  dct:title "Nature Care Products Standard" ;
