<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/555> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "A country brand is a strategy to position the image of a country on the international market. The aim is to boost the country’s reputation through tourism, investment, and the exports of goods and services.  Costa Rica projects itself to the world, integrally promoting tourism, investment, and exports, along with Costa Rican culture and uniqueness. Costa Rica is a country that has a lot to say, and our way of speaking to the world is done through our country brand, essential COSTA RICA. With the purpose of fulfilling the promise we have made to the world, we guarantee that the companies that use the country brand represent our core values:  •\tExcellence: businesses portray Costa Rican human talent through the specialization of goods and services.  •\tSustainability: through creative strategies, companies co-exist with the environment.  •\tInnovation: adjustments in the delivery of goods and services which aims to increase the rentability of the company.  •\tSocial Progress: companies that seek the well-being of their workers.  •\tCosta Rican bond: companies show their attachment to Costa Rican values.   The companies that represent these values, go through a thorough auditing process that grants the license of use of our country brand." ;
  dct:issued "1996"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://www.esencialcostarica.com/el-programa/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/555> ;
