<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/8082> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "We Care addresses companies in the food sector. The Standard stipulates holistic requirements for sustainability and provides a certification system for companies in this regard. It focuses on sustainability as a whole, namely: • ecological and social issues • entire product ranges, not just selected “flagship products” • sustainability at a company’s own sites as well as in the supply chain management We Care helps companies to systematically establish this responsibility, continuously develop it and make it credible and communicable by way of external inspection and certification. The value added within the food sector is globally interlinked. How can companies structure their management and value creation along the supply chain in a social, sustainable and fair manner while also providing credible evidence of this? We Care provides the answers. Food companies that import, process or produce food themselves, that arrange for food to be produced by other companies in addition or on an exclusive basis, or that distribute their raw materials or finished products as wholesalers or retailers as well, may be certified according to this Standard. There are already numerous systems for organic, fair and sustainability certification in terms of production of agricultural raw materials. That is why We Care primarily considers sustainability management in the subsequent steps of the value-added chain, e.g. for importers, manufacturers and brand owners. With the integrated focus on sustainable supply chain management, We Care is also geared towards promoting the implementation of producer-oriented organic, fair and sustainability certification in the supply chains. We Care covers the four action areas of Corporate Governance, Supply Chain Management, Environmental Management and Responsibility for Employees. Certification according to this Standard is evidence of the fact that the certified food company is acting in a social, sustainable and fair manner in accordance with verifiable criteria, including in particular in supply chain management. As part of the certification process, any equivalent subject-specific management system certifications the company already holds in the action areas of Environmental Management and Responsibility for Employees will be recognized in full as previous achievements in the audit and included in the certification. This ensures that any duplicate auditing is avoided." ;
  dct:created "2024-11-12"^^xsd:date ;
  dct:issued "2001"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <https://we-care-siegel.org/companies/?lang=en> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/8082> ;
  dct:title "We Care" ;
