<https://w3id.org/eudpp/standard/sustainability/898989> a eudpp:SustainabilityStandard ;
  dct:description "The ABVTEX Program is a sector effort led by the Brazilian Association of Textile Retail (ABVTEX), which represents the main fashion retail chains, including clothing, footwear, fashion accessories and textile goods for home (bed, table, bath and decoration). The main objective is to promote the best commercial practices with socio-environmental responsibility throughout the fashion value chain. At first, the ABVTEX Program was aimed only to suppliers and their subcontractors linked to the supply chain of the signatory retailers. However, as a natural evolution process and being an inclusive project, the facilities that are not part of the supply chain of the signatory retailers may join the Program, identifying and adopting good practices as a way of improving their socio-environmental responsibility, expanding their opportunities for business in the sector." ;
  dct:issued "1999"^^xsd:gYear ;
  dct:relation <http://www.abvtex.org.br/en/audit-manual/>, <http://www.abvtex.org.br/en/regulation-and-policies/>, <https://www.abvtex.org.br/en/full-checklist/> ;
  dct:source <https://www.standardsmap.org/en/factsheet/898989> ;
  dct:title "ABVTEX PROGRAM" ;
